an executive order from President Obama  could help millions pay off their  student loans he announced it today at  the University of Colorado Denver his  plan will let borrowers consolidate  their debt into a single government loan  at a lower rate  [Music]  as the cumulative total of student loan  borrowing approaches one trillion  dollars calls to forgive some or all of  that debt are mounting federally  guaranteed student loans make up more  than half that total and Barack Obama is  pushing to cap the amount any borrower  must pay back in a given year and to  forgive outstanding balances after 20  years among Occupy Wall Street  protesters calls to bail out student  loan holders are arguably the single  most voice demand and sites such as  forgive student loan debt beat the drum  for immediate and widespread relief but  forgiving student loan debt is a very  bad idea for at least three reasons  [Music]  about half of all college students take  out loans and when they do every lender  clearly spells out exactly how much  you're on the hook for and what your  monthly payments are gonna be after you  leave school critics say that eighteen  year olds don't understand what they're  getting into and shouldn't be held  accountable for their decisions but  that's an argument against letting kids  attend college not against letting them  borrow against future earnings to get a  degree that will increase lifetime  earnings by somewhere between about two  hundred and eighty thousand and one  million dollars while the cumulative  total of all college related debt is  huge it's not so big for individuals the  typical college graduate who borrowed  money to attend graduates owing about 25  grand they've got a minimum of 10 years  to pay back that amount and the  repayment schedule can be extended and  modified for a wide variety of reasons  the monthly payment for 25 grand in  student loans at going rates comes to  about 290 dollars a month that's not  chump change  but given that college grads have  unemployment rates that are less than  half the national average and that the  average salary offer for graduating  seniors is almost 50 grand the loan  amount isn't so bad either  I'm opposed to it like Tea Party  activist Occupy Wall Street protesters  are right to rail against bailouts for  big banks and financial institutions  that are politically connected but  student loan forgiveness advocates are  wrong to perpetuate yet another cycle of  balance it's never right to socialize  losses while privatizing games that's  what the banks did they erased their  money on stupid investments and then got  made whole at the expense of taxpayers  student loan forgiveness is simply  another version of the same swindle and  it offloads the cost of other people's  decisions on to taxpayers who guarantee  federally backed student loans College  is an important decision and it's made  even more expensive by heavily  subsidized loans but letting people off  the hook for loans they made with full  knowledge of the cost will not only  dissuade anyone from lending to students  who have no collateral other than their  future work output it will make it that  much harder to argue against the next  call for bailouts from the next group of  special interests for Reason TV I'm Nick  Gillespie  you
 

